      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand the heavy exhaustion of feeling like an empty shell, and while the language you use might feel poetic, the reality is that letting go only when the feelings become permanent usually signifies a crisis rather than a peaceful transition. It is a profound misunderstanding of reality to believe that the pain you describe is final or that continuing this way will bring genuine peace, because these feelings can be treated and changed with the right support. Please do not accept this void as your permanent reality; reaching out to a crisis line or mental health professional might seem noisy or unhelpful now, but they are actually the fastest way to find the genuine peace you are looking for when the burden lifts.",
